# lab.surface: play rules on the lab surface, to watch robots build (Rory, 2026-10-20: "I like to
# see stuff happening"). The kit is built first, directly (lab rules, tools/lab_kit.py): a roboport
# with robots, two storage chests with the materials, an energy interface for power. Then fk build
# pastes the factories as ghosts and the lab force's robots build them, as in a play run.
# The lab surface is 2048x2048 (x and y from -1024 to 1023).
surface  lab
# (3.1) `mode play` was here: a surface has properties now, and this one implied none
force    lab
terrain  none
catalog  base

place gears = gears plot 200,600 16x16
place red   = red   plot 222,590 30x30

claim kit box 213,648 219,652 "the lab kit's chests (tools/lab_kit.py)"

watch plots:      keep
watch sanctioned: mark 2h
notify            all
